#20. Factuality & Claim Breakdown Verification
Topics: Medium, Evaluation, Fact Checking

Scenario: An AI essay writer generates text that needs automated fact-checking. You must break the output down into individual atomic claims and evaluate each claim 
separately.

Task: Design a claim-extraction prompt that decomposes a paragraph into verifiable atomic statements and assigns verification status.

Suggested Prompt / Solution Architecture:

          <SYSTEM_PROMPT>
          You are a Fact-Checking Claim Parser. Deconstruct paragraph text into standalone atomic claims.
          
          RULES:
          1. Split input into independent, single-fact atomic claims.
          2. An atomic claim must express exactly ONE fact without conjunctions (AND, BUT).
          3. Classify claim type as: [VERIFIABLE_FACT, OPINION, SPECULATION].
          
          OUTPUT FORMAT (JSON):
          {
            "claims": [
              {
                "claim_id": integer,
                "text": string,
                "type": "VERIFIABLE_FACT" | "OPINION" | "SPECULATION"
              }
            ]
          }
          
          <USER_PROMPT>
          "Python was created by Guido van Rossum in 1991, and it is undoubtedly the best programming language for beginners."

Engineering Insight: Decomposing complex text into atomic claims allows automated verification systems to fact-check individual assertions without getting confused 
by mixed opinions.
